# Expected (line, col, len, role) for paren.id. HAND-WRITTEN from the law.
#
# What this fixture discriminates: the three-way paren split. All three are
# ONE role — `layout`, red and FAINT, because a paren is inferable from the
# shape of the line — and the split lives in the cards `strata`, `param` and
# `group`. gaps/GAP-078.md ruled that: the split never changes hue, so it is
# not a role, and §0g's demand that the three be distinguished is satisfied by
# the card, which is also what SPECIFICITY is measured over.
#
# GROUPING is decidable — grammar.md gives `primary -> "(" expr ")"` against
# `postfix -> "(" [args] ")"`, and the two differ by whether an operand
# precedes the paren — so line 3 is `group` twice. LEVEL versus PARAMETER is
# decided by the LADDER: §0.5 declares operation-first at the trie and calls
# subject-first at the value, and both mark a level the same way, by a SECOND
# group immediately following the first. `map(symbol)(u32)` carries that mark,
# so the first group is `strata` and the second is `param`. That reading is a
# card-level judgement and it is gated; at ROLE granularity, which is what
# these rows assert, both are `layout` either way.
#
# This is the ONE fixture that does not `duo check`: `map` is undeclared, and
# the two-level curried callable that would declare it is exactly the
# construct the fixture exists to be sharp about. The golden token corpus is
# LEXICAL — see docs/spec/roles.md §6. # gap[078]
spans = {
    { 1, 1, 8, "comment" },
    { 2, 1, 1, "place" },
    { 2, 3, 1, "operator" },
    { 2, 5, 3, "callable" },
    { 2, 8, 1, "layout" },
    { 2, 9, 6, "place" },
    { 2, 15, 1, "layout" },
    { 2, 16, 1, "layout" },
    { 2, 17, 3, "descriptor" },
    { 2, 20, 1, "layout" },
    { 3, 1, 1, "place" },
    { 3, 3, 1, "operator" },
    { 3, 5, 1, "layout" },
    { 3, 6, 1, "place" },
    { 3, 8, 1, "operator" },
    { 3, 10, 1, "place" },
    { 3, 11, 1, "layout" },
    { 3, 13, 1, "operator" },
    { 3, 15, 1, "place" },
}
